  },
  "note": "Triennial election, Monday 16 January 1911 (\"The Urban Council Elections take place on Monday\", Armagh Guardian, 13 January 1911, p. 2); all three wards were contested and the votes were counted in the City Hall on the Tuesday under Mr Lennon, returning officer. The paper prints initials and groups the candidates under party headings. The North Ward decided the majority on the council; the Nationalists held it by 26 votes at the margin."
